>> servings: 4
>> source: https://www.homegrown-kitchen.example/recipes/roast-pumpkin-soup-with-garlic-croutons
>> tags: Soup, Vegetarian, Weeknight

== Soup ==

Preheat the oven to 200°C. Toss the pumpkin, onion and @garlic{3%clove} with the oil on a large tray, season, and roast ~{35%minutes} until soft and browned at the edges. @Kent pumpkin{1.2%kg} @brown onion{1} @olive oil{2%tbsp}

Squeeze the @garlic{3%clove} from its skins into a large saucepan with the roasted vegetables, @bay leaf{=1} and stock. Simmer ~{10%minutes}. @vegetable stock{1%l}

Discard the @bay leaf{=1}. Blend until smooth, stir in the cream and season. @thickened cream{100%ml}

== Garlic croutons ==

Toss the bread with the oil and @garlic{1%clove}. Bake at 200°C for ~{8%minutes}, turning once, until golden. @sourdough{2%slice} @olive oil{1%tbsp}

Ladle the soup into warm bowls and top with the croutons and a grind of pepper.
